Square array T(m, n), read by ascending antidiagonals. Let f(k) = k/2 if k is even, otherwise ((2*n+1)*k + 2*T(m, n) + 1)/2, T(m, n) is the smallest integer greater than -1, where m = f^j(m) for j > 0 exists. f^j(m) means the j-th iterate of f(m).

The 89 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `0`.

